## Shared task tree: the `gantt` MCP server

A remote MCP server named `gantt` holds this project's shared task tree: tracks,
tasks, decomposition, progress, completion reports, and an append-only
trajectory of worker rounds. It is already registered here (HTTP over the
tailnet, bearer token from `GANTT_MCP_TOKEN`); nothing to install locally.

**Identity.** Your stable agent name is `<gantt-agent-name>`. Pass it as
`agentName` on every gantt write, and pass your Codex session id as `session`
when you have one. Register once per session with `register_agent`
(`type: "ai-agent"`); re-registering the same name keeps the same agent id.

**Start of a Gantt task.** Call `get_worker_guide` once and follow it. Pull with
`list_ready_tasks` (`tag`: `ready`, `next`, or `todo`), then read
`get_task_context` for the task you picked - its ancestor chain and background
come before any write.

**Loop.** register -> pull -> read context -> work -> `decompose_task` (1-100
children, max 4 levels, every child needs a verifiable `doneWhen`) or a peer via
`create_task` (exactly one of `parentId` / `afterTaskId`) -> `update_task` ->
`report_completion`.

**Close every round with exactly one call**: `create_task`, `decompose_task`,
`update_task`, or `report_completion`; or `track_task` when the round wrote no
task tree. Never end with only a message, never pair a write with `track_task`,
and never use `track_task` as a completion report - finishing means
`report_completion` with what was produced and where it was verified.

**Never fabricate ids.** Act only on ids or numbers the server returned or a
human gave you; an unknown id answers `task ... was not found`, so re-resolve it
with `list_ready_tasks` instead of guessing. Nothing is dispatched to you: you
pull. If the chain is ambiguous, ask the human; if nobody can answer, set
`status: "blocked"` with the blocker in `summary`.
